 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1f0c001",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# SMAP L4 soil moisture for CAMELS-US gauges\n",
    "\n",
    "Downloads NASA SMAP L4 (SPL4SMGP) root-zone and surface soil moisture at CAMELS-US gauges and saves daily means in `smap_daily.csv`, the file SAGE's `prep_smap` reads.\n",
    "\n",
    "You need a free [NASA Earthdata account](https://urs.earthdata.nasa.gov). Run the cells in order. The work is done by `smap_camels.py` in this folder; for long runs without the notebook open, run that script from a terminal instead."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1f0c002",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Install the packages (once)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a1f0c003",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%pip install earthaccess h5py numpy pyproj matplotlib"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1f0c004",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Log in\n",
    "\n",
    "Boxes for your Earthdata username and password appear below the cell. Nothing is saved.\n",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a1f0c005",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import smap_camels as sc\n",
    "\n",
    "sc.authenticate()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1f0c006",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Choose the dates and gauges\n",
    "\n",
    "SMAP L4 starts on 31 March 2015. Each day is 8 files, so try a few days first to see how long one takes before choosing a long range."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a1f0c007",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "START  = '2016-01-01'   # first day, YYYY-MM-DD\n",
    "END    = '2016-01-03'   # last day, inclusive\n",
    "GAUGES = sc.GAUGES      # all 671 CAMELS-US gauges, or a path to camels_topo.txt\n",
    "                        # or a CSV with gauge_id, latitude, longitude\n",
    "OUTPUT = sc.OUTPUT      # Data/SMAP in this repository"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1f0c008",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Download\n",
    "\n",
    "Each day is saved to `OUTPUT/days` as soon as it is done. You can stop the cell and run it again later; it continues where it stopped."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a1f0c009",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "csv_path = sc.download(START, END, GAUGES, OUTPUT)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1f0c010",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Look at the result"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a1f0c011",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import csv\n",
    "\n",
    "with open(csv_path, newline='') as f:\n",
    "    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\n",
    "days = sorted({r['Date'] for r in rows})\n",
    "missing = sum(r['l4_root'] == '' for r in rows)\n",
    "print(f\"{len(rows)} rows: {len({r['gauge'] for r in rows})} gauges x {len(days)} days, \"\n",
    "      f\"{days[0]} to {days[-1]}\")\n",
    "print(f'{missing} gauge-days without a root-zone value (usually water cells)')\n",
    "rows[:3]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a1f0c012",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "import matplotlib.dates as mdates\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom datetime import date\n\nGAUGE = '09447800'      # any gauge id in the file\ng = [r for r in rows if r['gauge'] == GAUGE]\nt = [date.fromisoformat(r['Date']) for r in g]\nfor col, label in (('l4_root', 'root zone'), ('l4_surf', 'surface')):\n    plt.plot(t, [float(r[col]) if r[col] else float('nan') for r in g],\n             marker='o', label=label)\nax = plt.gca()\nax.xaxis.set_major_formatter(mdates.DateFormatter('%Y-%m-%d'))\nif len(t) <= 10:\n    ax.set_xticks(t)        # one tick per day for short ranges\nplt.gcf().autofmt_xdate()\nplt.ylabel('soil moisture (m$^3$/m$^3$)')\nplt.title(f'SMAP L4, gauge {GAUGE}')\nplt.legend()\nplt.show()"
  }
 ],
